<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sixth Crusade</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1228">1228</a>–<a href="/years/1229">1229</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sixth <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusade">Crusade</a> (1228–1229) was led by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frederick-ii">Holy Roman Emperor Frederick II</a>, who sailed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/holy-land">Holy Land</a> while excommunicated by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-gregory-ix">Pope Gregory IX</a>. Without fighting a major battle he negotiated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-jaffa-1229">Treaty of Jaffa (1229)</a> with the Ayyubid sultan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-kamil">al-Kamil</a>, which returned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jerusalem">Jerusalem</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bethlehem">Bethlehem</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nazareth">Nazareth</a> to Christian rule for ten years. It was the only crusade after the First to regain Jerusalem.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sixth-crusade.jpg" alt="Sixth Crusade" width="191" height="393" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: anonymous · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Al-Kamil_Muhammad_al-Malik_and_Frederick_II_Holy_Roman_Emperor.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
